WEBVTT

00:01.712 --> 00:05.887
The optical storage device that you
acquired from the former spy, Kurogao,

00:06.429 --> 00:08.433
the results of my analysis show

00:08.433 --> 00:12.901
that it contains the guest list
for a Yozakura wedding reception.

00:12.901 --> 00:13.819
9TH YOZAKURA HEAD'S WEDDING RECEPTION

00:13.819 --> 00:15.489
The ninth head's, no less.

00:15.782 --> 00:19.455
In other words,
our parents' wedding reception.

00:19.455 --> 00:20.415
AKARI ASANO
HIDE ASANO

00:20.415 --> 00:24.675
The issue here is the fact
that your parents' names are on this list.

00:27.388 --> 00:29.977
It wasn't... an accident!

00:30.812 --> 00:31.855
Tanpopo.

00:33.149 --> 00:37.116
Who would have thought that your family
also fell victim to Tanpopo?

00:37.617 --> 00:38.703
Huh?

00:38.703 --> 00:40.873
What do you mean, my family also?

00:41.917 --> 00:45.340
They also killed Mutsumi's mother,
the previous head.

00:45.967 --> 00:46.719
SCANNING

00:46.719 --> 00:48.848
<i>"The Somei-yoshino Project"?</i>

00:49.975 --> 00:50.935
"OUTLINE AND CHALLENGES
OF THE SOMEI-YOSHINO PLAN"

00:51.102 --> 00:54.442
<i>Unfortunately, someinine
cannot be created synthetically.</i>

00:54.943 --> 00:58.993
<i>Therefore, in order
to mass-produce it as a bioweapon,</i>

00:58.993 --> 01:03.544
<i>as well as build a distribution network,
we currently need a someinine factory.</i>

01:04.045 --> 01:04.921
<i>In other words...</i>

01:05.673 --> 01:08.428
<i>Mutsumi Yozakura's heart.</i>

01:09.598 --> 01:12.771
It's a doping agent
that replicates the Yozakura blood.

01:14.649 --> 01:17.321
For an average person like myself...

01:25.630 --> 01:27.299
this is as good as it gets.

01:48.466 --> 01:51.055
Tormenting children isn't my style.

01:51.055 --> 01:53.268
I'll put you
out of your misery right away.

02:19.278 --> 02:21.533
Sorry I got here late, Taiyo.

02:23.161 --> 02:25.373
A Gold-rank spy.

02:26.042 --> 02:27.879
Shinzo Yozakura.

02:30.008 --> 02:31.970
Hey, but you're cute.

02:35.310 --> 02:36.522
I see.

02:37.189 --> 02:40.655
You do look like
Nanao's regenerative mechanism.

02:58.649 --> 02:59.483
Huh?

03:01.697 --> 03:03.826
Whoa!

03:10.715 --> 03:13.136
SHINZO

03:13.136 --> 03:15.223
<i>Enemy reinforcements could be on the way.</i>

03:15.473 --> 03:17.520
Leave this to me, Taiyo, and--

03:21.235 --> 03:23.114
You're a Yozakura, all right...

03:23.782 --> 03:26.495
to actually compete
with this body of mine.

03:26.663 --> 03:27.957
But you see...

03:31.130 --> 03:34.763
what if I were to press
the switch embedded in my tooth...

03:35.347 --> 03:39.480
<i>and blow up this hotel,
civilian guests and all?</i>

03:42.402 --> 03:45.534
To ensure that I won't grit my teeth...

03:46.202 --> 03:48.999
<i>you know what it is
that you need to do...</i>

03:50.628 --> 03:52.172
<i>...right?</i>

03:56.430 --> 03:58.309
Yes. That's right.

03:58.769 --> 04:01.273
You need to grit your own teeth.

04:10.710 --> 04:17.849
YOZAKURA FAMILY

05:34.293 --> 05:39.679
PLAN 15
YOZAKURA BLOOD

05:41.265 --> 05:42.100
What's going on?

05:45.691 --> 05:47.820
Well, you're tough beyond belief.

05:48.446 --> 05:52.622
But since you can't fight back,
there's no point in enduring it.

05:52.622 --> 05:54.584
So why don't you just resign yourself
and die?

05:56.086 --> 05:58.592
I don't want to die,
because I'm afraid to.

05:59.092 --> 06:02.057
And besides,
it's not like I'm enduring anything.

06:03.142 --> 06:06.065
I'm just waiting, that's all.

06:07.693 --> 06:08.695
Waiting?

06:08.695 --> 06:09.614
<i>Owner!</i>

06:10.156 --> 06:11.993
This is Front Desk Number Two!

06:11.993 --> 06:15.166
There's a terrorist on a rampage,
and it's total chaos here!

06:16.544 --> 06:20.301
Welcome to this five-star hotel!

06:21.345 --> 06:24.936
<i>Saving human lives
is the top priority in any mission.</i>

06:25.436 --> 06:26.856
<i>Do whatever it takes.</i>

06:29.529 --> 06:31.115
All right, then.

06:31.115 --> 06:35.498
Let me show you first-class hospitality
as I escort you to heaven!

06:35.708 --> 06:39.757
I'm offering a bloodbath for those of you
in the highest tax bracket!

06:40.759 --> 06:42.513
NANAO ROCKETS
FIREWORKS THAT RESEMBLE SPARKS

06:42.722 --> 06:47.230
All you celestial beings,
I'm inviting you to take a tour of hell!

06:54.912 --> 06:56.875
EXTREME FLUFF-FLUFF
CAN ENVELOP UP TO 100-METER RADIUS

07:00.298 --> 07:01.175
All right.

07:05.642 --> 07:07.855
Come on, Tama! Let's get out of here!

07:14.827 --> 07:18.000
You saved us! Thank you!

07:19.377 --> 07:21.215
<i>We're still confirming this,</i>

07:21.215 --> 07:24.179
<i>but miraculously,
it seems like everyone was evacuated.</i>

07:28.730 --> 07:33.155
Claiming that this knockoff
gives you the Yozakuras' powers,

07:33.155 --> 07:34.659
that's an insult to my family.

07:34.659 --> 07:35.869
JUST GLOVES
IRON GLOVES KNITTED BY FUTABA

07:35.869 --> 07:37.497
I'll make you eat those words.

07:40.294 --> 07:45.179
So you say, but if you
can't even finish off this knockoff...

07:46.098 --> 07:47.016
Huh?

07:51.860 --> 07:56.828
Version Zero Super-size
Yozakura Electric Gun Spring Thunder.

07:58.623 --> 08:01.671
Due to its complex build
and vicious recoil,

08:01.671 --> 08:04.844
I'm the only one in our family
who can fire it.

08:07.725 --> 08:10.313
I admit that it looks
like it packs a devastating punch.

08:11.356 --> 08:13.027
But do you really think

08:13.027 --> 08:16.784
such a flaw-riddled ace in the hole
would work on me?

08:18.120 --> 08:19.456
Bring it on.

08:19.456 --> 08:20.876
I'll sidestep it with ease.

08:25.969 --> 08:28.725
We hacked the detonator and the camera.

08:32.315 --> 08:36.281
<i>You didn't lose because you confronted me.</i>

08:37.367 --> 08:39.830
<i>It was because you overlooked
my younger brother.</i>

08:42.418 --> 08:43.838
You've got me there.

08:52.648 --> 08:53.775
Thunder?

08:54.276 --> 08:56.280
But it's so sunny out. How could that be?

09:11.644 --> 09:14.149
Such fine men, aren't you?

09:25.296 --> 09:27.760
So a fake doesn't cut it, after all, huh?

09:28.928 --> 09:32.018
But I got plenty of data, so...

09:32.435 --> 09:35.483
for now, Nohmen, good work.

09:37.153 --> 09:38.447
And now...

09:39.533 --> 09:41.495
just leave the rest to the real deal.

09:45.127 --> 09:49.094
Oh, man. I was so scared!

09:50.179 --> 09:52.601
<i>Good job, Big Bro Shinzo!</i>

09:53.102 --> 09:55.189
I've subdued the enemy.

09:55.189 --> 09:57.653
<i>I'm heading your way now.</i>

09:58.362 --> 09:59.364
Roger that.

10:09.384 --> 10:10.887
I see that you're injured.

10:11.388 --> 10:12.348
Are you all right?

10:14.729 --> 10:16.524
Thank you very much.

10:18.737 --> 10:21.116
<i>There was still someone in the hotel?</i>

10:22.828 --> 10:24.665
You should take care of yourself.

10:25.458 --> 10:28.965
If you have a weak body, you can't even
protect the one you want to protect.

10:33.641 --> 10:35.604
Taiyo! There you are!

10:35.937 --> 10:36.898
Big Bro Shinzo!

10:37.398 --> 10:40.572
I knew that you'd have my back, Taiyo.

10:41.031 --> 10:42.283
Thanks, man.

10:44.538 --> 10:47.001
Taiyo, what's that?

10:47.001 --> 10:47.961
Huh?

10:57.313 --> 10:59.317
Taiyo! Hey!

11:01.572 --> 11:02.908
Hang in there!

11:03.283 --> 11:05.496
Taiyo! Taiyo!

11:06.164 --> 11:08.293
Taiyo! Taiyo!

11:09.254 --> 11:10.841
Taiyo!

11:12.970 --> 11:17.980
YOZAKURA FAMILY

11:21.821 --> 11:24.827
He's been shot all over his body,
mainly in the internal organs,

11:24.827 --> 11:25.912
more than a dozen times.

11:26.831 --> 11:28.877
He's made it out of the woods somehow...

11:29.670 --> 11:34.178
but if it hadn't been for Big Bro Shinzo's
first aid, it would have been too late.

11:41.986 --> 11:43.155
Taiyo...

11:44.783 --> 11:48.625
He won't be regaining consciousness
anytime soon, so he needs absolute--

11:50.419 --> 11:52.048
Hey, that really hurt, Futaba.

11:52.048 --> 11:54.093
I was only trying to lighten things up.

11:54.595 --> 11:56.348
Inappropriate time and place.

11:56.724 --> 11:58.728
I held back
because we're in the infirmary.

11:58.728 --> 11:59.772
Be thankful.

12:00.815 --> 12:03.821
Except for family, no visitors allowed.

12:03.821 --> 12:05.157
Even though I'm the eldest son?

12:06.034 --> 12:10.627
NANAO'S ROOM

12:12.421 --> 12:14.092
Okay, everyone, let's go.

12:14.092 --> 12:17.849
He can't get the rest he needs
with too many attendants around.

12:19.770 --> 12:24.195
Big Sis Mutsumi, I'm leaving this box
of medical equipment with you.

12:24.697 --> 12:26.534
If anything happens, use it.

12:27.284 --> 12:29.455
Thanks, Nanao.

13:12.208 --> 13:13.669
Whoops.

13:41.015 --> 13:44.146
Big Bro... do you have a minute?

13:52.204 --> 13:53.833
Don't be too hard on yourself, Shinzo.

13:54.458 --> 13:55.795
It's not your fault.

13:58.049 --> 13:59.928
It's not that, Big Bro.

14:02.474 --> 14:04.855
I still can't believe it myself.

14:05.857 --> 14:09.948
At that moment, right before my eyes...

14:10.449 --> 14:12.662
there was Taiyo,
suddenly drenched in blood.

14:14.040 --> 14:18.089
With my hearing, I never miss
any silencers or snipers,

14:18.799 --> 14:22.557
and I didn't detect anyone's presence
there, let alone murderous intent.

14:23.183 --> 14:25.605
So the only thing I can think of...

14:26.189 --> 14:29.613
is that Taiyo had already
been attacked before I got there...

14:30.197 --> 14:34.497
and that was his body's
delayed reaction to it.

14:35.374 --> 14:37.629
That's too ridiculous to be true.

14:38.714 --> 14:44.100
But there's just one person that I know
who's capable of that.

14:57.669 --> 15:01.092
Why this sudden chirping
when it's not to mark the time?

15:04.056 --> 15:05.893
It's an intruder alarm.

15:05.893 --> 15:07.146
Intruder?

15:07.564 --> 15:12.322
The type of chirp indicates
the number of intruders on the premises.

15:12.699 --> 15:15.328
You mean the alarm changes
depending on the enemy?

15:15.328 --> 15:18.084
Yeah. A crow means less than ten people.

15:18.084 --> 15:20.005
A rooster means less than a hundred.

15:20.965 --> 15:22.217
Then...

15:26.017 --> 15:27.269
what if it's a bush warbler?

15:27.937 --> 15:29.816
When it's a bush warbler...

15:32.822 --> 15:34.618
there are more than a thousand.

15:41.005 --> 15:42.675
Just can't wait.

15:42.675 --> 15:44.679
I'm gonna go ahead and bust in!

15:44.679 --> 15:46.850
Hey! We're supposed to stand by!

15:46.850 --> 15:47.685
Shut up!

15:48.186 --> 15:50.525
My body's itching to go!
I can't stop myself!

15:51.819 --> 15:54.616
Don't disrupt the order.

15:55.283 --> 15:58.206
<i>Hey, Yama, those compatibles are valuable.</i>

15:58.707 --> 16:00.085
<i>Don't break them, okay?</i>

16:00.085 --> 16:01.713
Forgive me.

16:03.049 --> 16:07.266
But some become brutal due to
the side effects of their compatibility.

16:07.266 --> 16:09.938
If I let my guard down,
my leadership will soon be undermined.

16:09.938 --> 16:11.023
YAMA CAPTAIN OF
THE HAZAKURA BATTALION

16:11.733 --> 16:14.948
Do your best to make this a success,

16:14.948 --> 16:17.745
since it was actually kind of a hassle.

16:18.706 --> 16:23.966
We lured a Yozakura in and found that,
on his own, he could be taken out.

16:24.759 --> 16:27.222
If anyone in the family
sustains any injuries,

16:27.515 --> 16:29.728
all of the siblings
would gather at the mansion,

16:29.978 --> 16:32.065
making it hard for them to escape.

16:32.399 --> 16:36.783
Now we can get rid of all of the Yozakuras
in our way, except for Mutsumi, in one go.

16:37.577 --> 16:38.746
Now get going.

16:40.541 --> 16:42.211
Hazakura Battalion...

16:46.135 --> 16:48.139
Our security's been breached.

16:48.139 --> 16:49.266
What do you mean?

16:50.393 --> 16:57.407
Looks like our guests managed to find
our security codes somewhere.

17:44.586 --> 17:46.047
M-Monster!

17:46.548 --> 17:47.800
Don't panic.

17:48.343 --> 17:50.305
That's just a guard dog.

17:51.390 --> 17:55.023
The real monsters
are about to show up now.

17:56.651 --> 18:00.492
We have an injured person
among us at the moment.

18:03.624 --> 18:05.377
So I'm going to have to ask you to leave.

18:06.045 --> 18:09.218
Hey, Futaba, you bashed me
with your full strength, didn't you?

18:09.218 --> 18:11.598
My teeth are feeling loose in the back.

18:15.063 --> 18:15.940
Let's go!

18:41.658 --> 18:43.453
Whoa! Stay away!

19:04.244 --> 19:07.710
I see. They're as pesky
as you said, Shinzo.

19:08.336 --> 19:11.885
Normally, when I toss someone,
they're out cold for at least a full day.

19:12.803 --> 19:14.807
My tranquilizers aren't working, either!

19:15.308 --> 19:18.649
No matter how many bullets I bombard
them with, they refuse to budge!

19:18.941 --> 19:21.738
Tough or not, a scrub is a scrub!

19:21.738 --> 19:24.159
Hand-to-hand combat is like life!

19:25.119 --> 19:26.790
Moving forward is the only option!

19:27.667 --> 19:30.589
I've only heard that
about ten thousand times.

19:31.591 --> 19:32.760
Stand your ground.

19:33.762 --> 19:36.643
First Unit, divert the siblings
to the front of the house.

19:37.143 --> 19:40.275
Second Unit, Third Unit,
storm the mansion.

19:40.400 --> 19:42.195
Roger that!

19:45.285 --> 19:47.038
The eldest son's a tough foe!

19:47.038 --> 19:48.625
- Everyone charge him at once!
- Right!

19:54.428 --> 19:55.764
Mist Coccoon!

19:58.144 --> 19:59.271
"Tough foe," huh?

19:59.814 --> 20:01.442
I feel so underrated.

20:02.360 --> 20:05.450
You can't even get near the mansion.

20:05.993 --> 20:08.122
I shouldn't even
have to lift my own finger.

20:12.590 --> 20:15.219
How are we supposed to deal
with a monster like this?

20:15.596 --> 20:18.309
Captain! We can't hold out any longer!

20:18.309 --> 20:20.063
Not yet. Draw him in!

20:20.564 --> 20:24.154
Three percent is the maximum Hazakura
compatibility rate for normal people.

20:24.656 --> 20:28.204
Not even Nohmen, who boasts 10%,
could stack up against them.

20:31.586 --> 20:36.721
Even with 60%-plus power, you can't
let your guard down against them.

20:38.224 --> 20:40.646
As a dog lover, this is painful.

20:41.146 --> 20:44.319
But it's for the sake of Tanpopo.

20:59.433 --> 21:00.644
Goliath!

21:04.276 --> 21:06.948
So you deactivated Mist Cocoon
after all, huh?

21:07.490 --> 21:10.455
Otherwise, the dog would have
been caught in the crossfire, too.

21:10.956 --> 21:14.672
But that's what got me into the mansion.

21:15.173 --> 21:17.678
To think that the most powerful family's
greatest weakness

21:17.678 --> 21:19.264
would be love for family.

21:19.264 --> 21:20.851
How ironic.

21:22.730 --> 21:25.026
Our family's really close.

21:25.611 --> 21:28.784
And so I won't let you die an easy death.

21:33.668 --> 21:35.589
<i>Transmitter noise in my speaker?</i>

21:36.090 --> 21:38.804
<i>Not only that, but it's
being jammed indiscriminately?</i>

21:42.185 --> 21:44.272
Activate Hibernation.

21:51.078 --> 21:52.455
The walls?

21:58.342 --> 22:01.265
Farewell, monsters.

22:07.402 --> 22:08.320
Kyoichiro!

22:10.701 --> 22:11.536
That voice...

22:12.120 --> 22:13.080
Don't panic.

22:13.582 --> 22:16.378
They're not out to kill Mutsumi.

22:19.594 --> 22:24.604
Either way, Hibernation can only
be disabled with the head's ring.

22:25.564 --> 22:27.275
I'll leave the Tanpopo battalion to you.

22:28.528 --> 22:34.540
I'm going to get the previous head's ring
back from him.

24:06.599 --> 24:07.976
YOZAKURA BLOOD

24:09.104 --> 24:10.982
NEXT TIME
CLEANING THE YARD
